===Etymology 1===
{{root|nl|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|id=cut}}
From {{inh|nl|dum|schēren}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|skeran}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*skeran}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*skeraną}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut}}.

====Verb====
{{nl-verb}}

# {{lb|nl|transitive|reflexive}} to [[shave]] (reflexive pronouns are used for self-directed actions)
#: {{uxi|nl|hij scheert zich nu|he's shaving now}}
#: {{uxi|nl|de arts scheerde de huid rond de wond van de patiënt|the doctor shaved the skin around the patient's wound}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[shear]]
#: {{uxi|nl|morgen gaan ze de schapen scheren|they will shear the sheep tomorrow}}

